import json
from pathlib import Path
from porto import ROOT, OUT
p=OUT/'porto-all-10m'
r=json.loads((p/'benchmark.json').read_text())
names={'colour_recovery':'Our colour recovery','golden_muscat':'Golden-Muscat','loam':'LOAM mode 6 / strips','jvp_resampled':'JVP coarse output resampled'}
lines=['# Porto: all six hazards at 10 x 10 m','',
'All recovery outputs and reference comparisons now use 10 m cell centres, with no 250 m averaging. Twenty-four GeoTIFFs contain six hazards for four methods. Each TIFF is EPSG:31982, has 10 m pixels and uses 255 for unknown; codes 0..9 map to risk-bin midpoints (code+0.5)/10. Source images still provide approximately 30 m detail; resampling creates correlated smaller cells, not new observations.','',
'## Matched test comparison','',
'Equal-hazard averages over the existing physical 3 km test blocks. Previously examined maps: retrospective, not blind. Correct-and-present divides correctly classified cells by all eligible reference cells; missing predictions are unsuccessful.','',
'| Method | Correct and present | Missing | High-risk recall |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for m in names:
 s=r['test_macro'][m];lines.append(f"| {names[m]} | {s['exact_all_pct']:.2f}% | {s['missing_pct']:.2f}% | {s['high_recall_pct']:.2f}% |")
lines+=['','Our colour recovery no longer leads the broad-class agreement metric: 63.31% versus 63.91% for resampled JVP. It recovers many more high-risk locations, but high-risk precision and unsupported coverage must also be considered. The old 79.22% score measured a different, coarser task; it does not describe these outputs.','',
'| Hazard | Eligible test cells | Correct | Missing | Correct and present |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for h,v in r['hazards'].items():
 s=v['methods']['colour_recovery']['test'];lines.append(f"| {h} | {s['eligible']} | {s['correct']} | {s['missing']} | {s['exact_all_pct']:.2f}% |")
lines+=['','## Definition and limits','',
'- Prediction: classify native PDF pixels with the frozen grey-blending model, then sample the nearest accepted source pixel at every 10 m centre. Rejected colours remain unknown. No cell averaging, filling or smoothing. The former eight-pixel support requirement for a 250 m mean is not applied.','- Reference: transform every 10 m centre to the numerical raster and take the native pixel containing it. A centre is eligible when that source pixel has data. The old >=15-pixel-per-cell criterion cannot be applied to subpixel grids.','- Five scoring classes have boundaries 0.2/0.4/0.6/0.8. Repeated subpixel values are correlated; millions of cells do not mean millions of independent measurements.','- Golden-Muscat and LOAM use their saved frozen source-pixel predictions; networks were not retrained or rerun. Their original configuration limitations remain.','- JVP is the shipped coarse output copied onto smaller cells. It gains no geometric detail. Its intended legend step is round(value*9), matching the previous class-decoding rule. Its reported MAE in JSON uses that rounded bin midpoint, not the original continuous stored value.','- DIGMAPPER remains unscored because no predictions were produced.','- Reference PNGs come from the same author; original TIFF provenance is unauthenticated. No numeric-reference values enter the recovery.','- Predictions where reference is absent are recorded separately, not counted as correct or wrong in class agreement. The JSON includes counts, confusion matrices, value error and high-risk precision.','- Richfield source-vector exports remain vectors; they never used a 250 m aggregation grid. This rebenchmark concerns the six Porto layers.','',
'## Files and checks','',
'Each hazard folder contains colour_recovery.tif, golden_muscat.tif, loam.tif and jvp_resampled.tif. benchmark.json contains every count, output hash and per-hazard/all/test metric.','',
'Verified all exported TIFF arrays by readback, including 10 m georeferencing. The full extent contains all valid native reference pixel centres. The new heat output exactly matches the existing requested 10 m heat overlay, with unknown padding outside it. Confusion-matrix totals equal eligible denominators.','',
'Reproduce: run benchmark_10m_all.py with model-trials/uiuc/.venv/Scripts/python.exe, then write_10m_report.py. All writes go to outputs/porto-all-10m; previous outputs remain available.']
(p/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{h.capitalize()}</td><td>{v["methods"]["colour_recovery"]["test"]["exact_all_pct"]:.1f}%</td></tr>' for h,v in r['hazards'].items())
bars=''.join(f'<div class="row"><div class="label"><span>{names[m]}</span><b>{r["test_macro"][m]["exact_all_pct"]:.1f}%</b></div><div class="track"><div style="width:{r["test_macro"][m]["exact_all_pct"]}%;background:var(--chart-{i+1});height:18px"></div></div></div>' for i,m in enumerate(names))
html='<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-sans);color:var(--foreground)}p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted-foreground)}.row{margin:15px 0}.label{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:5px}.track{height:18px;background:var(--secondary);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}table{width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{text-align:left;padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}</style></head><body><strong>10 m comparison — correct class and present</strong><p>All six Porto hazards · same locations for every method · equal-hazard averages</p>'+bars+'<p>10 m sampling without 250 m averaging. Source detail remains approximately 30 m. JVP is a resampled coarse baseline; the other methods use source-pixel predictions. DIGMAPPER has no score.</p><table><tr><th>Our recovery by hazard</th><th>Correct and present</th></tr>'+rows+'</table><p>Retrospective evaluation against same-author raster derivatives. Missing predictions count as failures. This measures broad risk classes, not exact boundary overlap.</p></body></html>'
(p/'comparison.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
print(p/'REPORT.md')
